  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The inductors of two <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></math> circuits are placed next to each other, as shown in the figure. The values of the self-inductance of the inductors, resistances, mutual-inductance and applied voltages are specified in the given circuit. After both the switches are closed simultaneously, the total work done by the batteries against the induced <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>F</mi></math> in the inductors by the time the currents reach their steady-state values is_______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mJ</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0007_ee4e2a0e1d4b.png\"/></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "55",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0007_dfebb381ba74.png\"/></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">1</mn></msub><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">+</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msub><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">1</mn></msub><msub><mi>i</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">1</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">d</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">i</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msub><msub><mi>i</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">d</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">i</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">+</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">i</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">1</mn></msub><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">·</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">i</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mJ</mi></math>,</p><p>Note : If mutual induction is taken in opposite direction then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mJ</mi></math></p>"
  }
